From b62a666b561732b1f732fcc61f723b19b555c6fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 15:29:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03107/11362] [outer-loop] B2: define the action metric
 unambiguously (A3 false-win lesson)

A3 produced a false win by comparing treatment actions_to_first_levelup (2984)
vs baseline total actions (7760). B2 must pick ONE metric, measure BOTH
conditions on it, record it for the baseline (currently total-only), and
CI-guard against a treatment reporting a different action field than the
baseline. Competition scores total actions -> canonical = total on solved games
unless a stop-at-final-levelup policy is adopted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 research-roadmap.yaml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/research-roadmap.yaml b/research-roadmap.yaml
index 1fb3cccc0a..6bf9ee8630 100644
--- a/research-roadmap.yaml
+++ b/research-roadmap.yaml
@@ -548,7 +548,7 @@ tasks:
          a. `.venv/bin/python -c "from carnot.agentic import arc_solver_kit as k; k.offline_arcade()"` exits 0.
          b. `.venv/bin/python {project_root}/scripts/kaggle/arc_local_submission_gate.py --help` exits 0 (the gate runs).
          Missing -> honest_verdict blocked_<resource>, EXIT. (--no-cov on focused pytest.)
-      1. Pin CORE from the baseline + expose a --lever <name> attribution slot. Do NOT revert to a raw solved-count verdict (that is the bug B2 protects against).
+      1. Pin CORE from the baseline + expose a --lever <name> attribution slot. Do NOT revert to a raw solved-count verdict (that is the bug B2 protects against). DEFINE THE ACTION METRIC UNAMBIGUOUSLY -- A3 (exp4513, flagged_adversarial) produced a FALSE WIN by comparing the treatment's `actions_to_first_levelup` (median 2984) against the baseline's `actions` total (median 7760): two different metrics. Pick ONE metric, measure BOTH conditions on it, and record it for the baseline (the baseline currently records `actions` total only, `actions_to_first_levelup`=None). The competition scores total actions to the reached level, so the canonical gate metric is TOTAL actions on solved games unless/until a stop-at-final-levelup policy is adopted; either way baseline and treatment MUST use the identical field. CI-guard against a treatment reporting a different action field than the baseline.
       2. CI-guard the four fixtures (A1->FAIL, A2->FAIL, POS->PASS, NEUTRAL->PASS) so the CORE-containment property can never silently regress; guard the baseline + game set against silent movement (cherry-pick guard).
       3. MEASURE the headroom budget B* (smallest budget where baseline solved_set(B) == solved_set(1.5B) across {8000,12000,16000,24000}) and set it as the canonical --budget default -- do NOT guess a value (a blind cap raise can mask a real slowdown). Until measured, the default stays 8000.
       4. Asserting tests (--no-cov). Emit a sample dashboard row (median_actions_on_core + core_solves_preserved + bonus) so A1-A6 report identically.
